+    "habitats": ["Urban", "Stockyard"],
+    "sections": {
+      "Printed source": "Wizards of the Coast, Curse of Strahd, first printing, march 2016, Chapter 5, The Town of Vallaki, N5 Arasek Stockyard, p. 115. Inherits the Saber-Toothed Tiger stat block in the 2014 Monster Manual, p. 336. https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/cos/the-town-of-vallaki#AreasofVallaki",
+      "Traits": "Keen Smell. The tiger has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks based on scent.\nPounce. Move at least 20 ft. straight toward a creature and hit it with Claw on that turn. The creature falls prone on a failed DC 14 Strength save. A prone target can then be bitten once as a bonus action.",
+      "Actions": "Bite. Melee weapon attack, +6 to hit, 5 ft. reach, one target. A hit deals 10 (1d10 + 5) piercing damage.\nClaw. Melee weapon attack, +6 to hit, 5 ft. reach, one target. A hit deals 12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage.",
+      "Encounter application": "The tiger was trained to hunt Vistani servants of Strahd, per the p. 115 erratum. If released, it can track Rictavio or Piccolo by scent. Rictavio can stop an attack and coax it into the wagon. During the Tyger, Tyger event on pp. 123–124, it roams until hurt, then attacks the perceived source of the harm.",
+      "Encounter ecology": "Rictavio keeps the tiger in his carnival wagon in Vallaki and feeds it through the roof hatch.",
+      "Source notes": "The first printing replaces the base armor, HP, and challenge. It gives 84 HP without a replacement Hit Dice formula.\nThe printed base block gives +6 to hit and +5 damage on both attacks. The adventure does not change either value.\nPublisher errata changes p. 115 to target Strahd’s Vistani servants and removes recognition by scent and clothing from that paragraph. Page 116 of the first printing describes broader targeting and is not separately amended in the errata."
+    }
